<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP December coal output down 11 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP December coal output down 11 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd said on Monday its production of coal in Queensland fell 11 percent in December to 1.64 million tonnes from the year earlier period because of an equipment problem at the Saraji mine and industrial action at the Riverside site.</p>
<p>Year-to-date output for the seven months to Dec 31, saw an 11 percent rise year-on-year to 13.43 million tonnes, BHP said.</p>
<p>Higher output of iron ore in Western Australia in response to customer demand lifted production by 10 percent in the first seven months of 1996/97 (June-May) to 31.6 million tonnes and seven percent in December to 4.2 million tonnes, BHP said.  </p>
